.TH SYS_VM_SLABS 2 "2026-05-09" "Substrate" "System Calls Manual"
.SH NAME
sys_vm_slabs \- query physical page use by allocation site
.SH LIBRARY
System library (libsys, \-lsys)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <sys/sysinfo.h>
.PP
.BI "int sys_vm_slabs(sys_slabinfo_t *" slabs ", size_t *" count ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR sys_vm_slabs ()
reports the kernel's page accounting table: one entry per kernel call
site that has allocated physical pages.
Each entry is a
.B sys_slabinfo_t :
.PP
.RS
.nf
typedef struct sys_slabinfo {
    char     name[32];
    uint32_t active;
    uint32_t total;
    uint32_t objsize;
    uint32_t slabs;
    uint32_t pages_per_slab;
} sys_slabinfo_t;
.fi
.RE
.PP
.TP
.I name
The call site: its kernel address,
.RI \(dq pc=0x ...\(dq,
for root; for anyone else only its position in the table,
.RI \(dq "site " N\(dq,
since a kernel text address shows where the kernel is loaded.
.TP
.I objsize
The page size.
.TP
.I total
Pages the site has allocated.
.TP
.I active
Pages it still holds.
.TP
.I slabs
Pages it has freed.
.TP
.I pages_per_slab
Always 1.
.PP
On entry
.I *count
is the array capacity; on return it is the number of entries written.
.SH RETURN VALUE
0 on success; on failure -1 and
.I errno
is set per the error contract.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
.I slabs
or
.I count
is NULL.
.TP
.B EFAULT
either pointer is unmapped.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sys_vm_stats (2),
.BR sys_vm_buffers (2),
.BR sysinfo (2)
